WEBVTT

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.860
Yes?

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:21.830
Good morning, ma'am.
It's Vincenzo. I'm here to pick him up.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:24.940
Good morning, Vinci.
Would you like to wait inside?

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:27.410
No, I'll wait here.

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:30.080
- Have you gotten the hang of work?
- Yes.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:33.480
Hurry and learn the ropes
so my husband can relax.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.990
Bruno! Vinci's waiting!

00:00:38.990 --> 00:00:40.420
Yeah.

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:46.860
I'll see you later,
Antonio. Study hard, now!

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:47.950
Yeah!

00:00:54.530 --> 00:01:02.170
Amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:17.020
I want to protect you and fulfill
my promise to the only one for me

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:24.360
In a world filled with doubt,
I still can't find the answer

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:31.940
Even so, I continue forward... Why?

00:01:31.940 --> 00:01:42.180
If I can change this dream-like
reality with my own two hands,

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:49.890
amid the difficulty of
sticking to that one feeling,

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:57.330
I want to protect the only one for me

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:05.170
I swear on my beating heart I will
continue to run until I burn away

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:12.380
Amid the eternal love
I feel simply by living,

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:20.410
I want to fulfill my promise

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.130
Is that all for this month?

00:02:34.130 --> 00:02:36.800
The guy in the back is the last one.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:40.870
You're scheduled to dine with
Cristiano-san this afternoon.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:42.680
Oh, that's right.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:47.280
Meanwhile, I'll go to Turin
and get our next car and number.

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.180
You've grown up to be quite helpful.

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.520
This is a busy job.
You pick things up fast.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:01.560
Business is booming, but body
disposal isn't very productive work.

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:06.900
If only people would solve their
conflicts with civilized discussion...

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:10.170
I agree with that...

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:13.170
...but sometimes killing is the easiest way.

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.140
Yeah. Sadly enough.

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.470
Then why do you do this work?

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:26.150
Can't raise a family on ideals alone...

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:30.210
It's sad.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:47.170
- Train rides sure are fun!
- Yeah!

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:50.230
- Lt's great that you got better!
- Yeah!

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:54.280
Hey. Angelica.

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:56.150
Yes, sir?

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.380
Have you taken your tablet?

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:00.380
No, not yet.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:04.650
Take it now, while there's time.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.170
Angelica's brought tablets with her?

00:04:14.170 --> 00:04:17.240
She can't kick her dependency yet.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.640
So her doctor prescribed some light pills.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:25.310
Be careful during this job.
For now, just keep an eye on her.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:26.870
Yes. I know.

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:38.490
"Angelica's Return"

00:04:50.670 --> 00:04:52.500
What are you going to do, Jean-san?

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:56.110
I'm going to hit up one of
my old acquaintances here.

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:58.240
The police, huh?

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:00.480
I'm going to use a different connection

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:03.180
to find out about Padania's "Milan Group."

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:06.310
Then we'll meet up at the hotel tonight.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.750
"Milan National and
Local Police Headquarters"

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:35.310
You can wait here.
I don't want to bother with explanations.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:36.840
Yes, sir.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.330
Inspector Moro. You have a visitor.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:55.170
It's not on my schedule.
Tell them to make an actual appointment.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:58.740
Actually, it's Sergeant Toni.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:00.440
Toni?

00:06:00.440 --> 00:06:03.310
"Leatherhead" Marco Toni?

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.250
Hey. What's "Leatherhead"?

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:16.360
The Central Security
Operations Service... NOCS.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:20.380
He's a pro who used to teach
practical combat skills here.

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:25.500
Hey, Marco!

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.520
Long time, no see!

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:31.570
It's good to see you doing well!

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:39.310
So, it's true that you quit
because you injured your eye?

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:41.280
What're you up to these days?

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.280
Doing odd jobs for the Cabinet Office.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:46.150
It's simple work.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:53.860
Pinocchio?

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:56.930
Doesn't ring a bell.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:03.170
He's the guy killing people
connected to the rich guy's trial in Milan.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:05.340
Oh, that.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:09.240
The F.R.F. Has too much influence here.

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.440
Rumor has it they're
greasing our commissioner's palm,

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:15.180
so we can't conduct
any serious investigations.

00:07:15.180 --> 00:07:19.320
Can you give me info?
Even someone on the bottom rung'll do.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:23.720
I don't know why
you're here, but I won't ask.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:24.760
Listen.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:29.280
I'm sure you know, but once you
step outside, watch out for pursuers.

00:07:36.340 --> 00:07:40.330
"Duomo"

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:48.450
I wonder if Angelica's working hard...

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:51.680
You certainly are
a curious person, Priscilla.

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:55.520
Coming all the way to Milan
on your time off to check on her...

00:07:55.520 --> 00:07:57.560
C'mon, you're worried too, Olga!

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:00.260
This being Angelica's
first outing in a while...

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:05.330
Do you think she's recovered
enough to do actual work?

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:08.630
We can't leave Marco-san
and Jean-san in charge.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:09.700
After all, Marco-san...

00:08:09.700 --> 00:08:13.230
What are you two doing here?

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:20.410
B-Buon giorno, Marco-san! Ciao, Ange!

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:23.310
Hello, Priscilla-san.

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:28.190
Actually, we just happened
to come here to do some shopping!

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.260
How are you feeling?

00:08:30.260 --> 00:08:33.230
Perfect timing. Switch seats with Olga.

00:08:33.230 --> 00:08:34.190
Eh?

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:39.900
The head of the separatists
sent someone after me

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:42.660
after I stopped by the local police.

00:08:43.870 --> 00:08:45.860
He just won't give up.

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:52.680
Okay, Olga! Use your ambassadorial
driving techniques to lose him!

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:54.150
You got it!

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:06.750
"Sforza Castle"

00:09:11.230 --> 00:09:13.600
Okay. Now what do we do?

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:19.170
Since you're here, you can
help out. I assume you're armed?

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:21.330
Yes. Handguns, at least...

00:09:23.380 --> 00:09:24.610
Angelica.

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:25.540
Yes, sir?

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:28.810
Give that case to Priscilla.

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:29.780
Eh?!

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:33.180
You can simply watch today.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:39.930
I-I'm fine!

00:09:39.930 --> 00:09:42.460
Submachine guns aren't my thing!

00:09:42.460 --> 00:09:45.790
Just take it! This isn't a game!

00:09:48.070 --> 00:09:52.830
"Naviglio River, Milan"

00:09:58.210 --> 00:10:01.210
Hurry, now. Tell me what you know.

00:10:01.210 --> 00:10:05.650
We don't know anything!
We just run errands!

00:10:05.650 --> 00:10:08.420
But you do know where
I can find the higher-ups.

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:11.260
I should mention I have
an itchy trigger finger.

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:15.630
Especially when I'm
dealing with trash like you.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.930
Okay! I'll talk!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:21.230
There's an apartment
our bosses use as a "nest"!

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:24.100
Good! Now give me details.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:40.580
Angelica!

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:45.820
What are you doing?!

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.820
Let's go!

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.540
I can take a break
from work after today.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:09.820
Now I can finally
go on vacation with my son.

00:11:09.820 --> 00:11:12.350
Easter is coming up.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:14.750
Thank you for all of
your recent hard work.

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.820
Don't you think you've
been killing a bit much lately?

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:20.390
It's getting hard to keep up.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:23.200
The government started it.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.700
They've been illegally arresting us

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:31.300
and now they're trying to
revise the law to make it legal.

00:11:31.300 --> 00:11:34.510
You mean the revised
Anti-Terrorist Special Measures Law?

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:38.180
Things are going to get ugly...

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:43.850
Yes. Milan may become
the Belfast of the 21st century.

00:11:43.850 --> 00:11:47.750
If that happens,
the fighting will last half a century

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:51.120
until both sides are worn down.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:55.930
Irredeemable fools exist in all times.

00:11:55.930 --> 00:11:58.400
Words don't get through to such people.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:09.740
When your vacation is over,
could you go and visit Pinocchio?

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:16.210
I think it might be best if you go.
The boy wants to hear from you.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:20.520
He's an adult now.
Some independence is best for him.

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:25.550
A parent is still a parent,
whatever age a child may be.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:33.630
Well, I should be going.
I need to pick up Vinci in Turin.

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:52.320
How does it look?

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:57.220
It's registered as an
auto parts subcontractor.

00:12:57.220 --> 00:13:01.530
People only use the fourth floor;
all other floors appear to be empty.

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:06.400
This "nest" seems to have four
or five people in it at all times.

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:07.870
What shall we do?

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:09.900
That many is no problem at all.

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:14.140
Priscilla. Take out the stun
grenades in the instrument case.

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:17.240
Yikes! You've been
carrying that stuff around?!

00:13:17.240 --> 00:13:20.340
Of course we have! This isn't a game!

00:13:31.560 --> 00:13:33.690
Whoa...

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:36.800
No need for talk, I see...

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:40.530
What? Did you expect we'd ring
the doorbell and have a chat?

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:05.350
Priscilla! It's all right!
You can come in now!

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:20.540
The two of us can stay here, Angelica.

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.150
Angelica?

00:14:35.590 --> 00:14:37.890
Angelica! Are you okay?!

00:14:37.890 --> 00:14:40.880
Are you tired? You should rest.

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:12.460
Don't do that, Ange!

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:15.790
It hurts when you grab that hard.

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:17.230
Okay?

00:15:34.680 --> 00:15:38.270
Let go of my arm, Ange...

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:42.820
Okay?

00:15:49.230 --> 00:15:50.420
Angelica!

00:16:01.340 --> 00:16:04.210
Marco-san...

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:06.850
Angelica! What's wrong?!

00:16:06.850 --> 00:16:11.280
Medicine... Medicine, please...

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:24.460
Is it her dependency?!

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:25.900
I don't know.

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:28.330
She's been taking her medicine

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:30.700
exactly as her conditioning
doctor instructed, but...

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:39.910
Olga. Toss these men
into the car downstairs.

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:41.350
Right.

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:43.310
Marco-san...

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:45.720
Priscilla! You all right?!

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:50.820
Please don't tell
Jean-san about Angelica...

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:52.760
What?

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:59.860
If he hears about this,
she'll be hospitalized again!

00:16:59.860 --> 00:17:01.860
I feel so bad for her!

00:17:04.000 --> 00:17:10.370
She's done nothing wrong.
We're the ones to blame here!

00:17:17.020 --> 00:17:19.520
She seems to be fine.

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:22.550
It must've been the anxiety
of her first real action in a while.

00:17:22.550 --> 00:17:26.820
If she seems fine when she
wakes up, give her a gun.

00:17:26.820 --> 00:17:29.460
That should help calm her nerves.

00:17:29.460 --> 00:17:31.400
What will we do now?

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:34.630
Threaten our captives until
they call their higher-ups.

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:38.600
We'll call for help from Rome
and clean house before dawn.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:40.370
Understood.

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:48.780
I hear Priscilla broke some bones.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:51.920
I'll admit, she endured it well.

00:17:51.920 --> 00:17:54.920
She's stronger than she looks.

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:58.460
She says it's "the power of love," though.

00:17:58.460 --> 00:18:01.460
Maybe she's just stupid after all.

00:18:01.460 --> 00:18:03.330
Priscilla said it herself.

00:18:03.330 --> 00:18:07.870
"Ange turned out that way
because Marco-san lacked love."

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:10.000
What's that supposed to mean?

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:14.770
This is Ange's first job in a while.
You need to treat her nicely.

00:18:14.770 --> 00:18:18.680
You can say things like that
because you're in the outfield.

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:21.110
Priscilla was sulking, you know.

00:18:21.110 --> 00:18:23.820
She kept calling her name out in vain,

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:26.720
but she regained her senses
when she heard your voice.

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:42.930
What a waste, fainting
on a big trip like this...

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:48.300
No, it's okay. Marco-san
was nice to me because of it!

00:18:53.710 --> 00:18:56.810
Say, Rico. Can I ask you a favor?

00:18:56.810 --> 00:18:58.180
What is it?

00:18:59.280 --> 00:19:02.050
Let me kill an enemy tomorrow.

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:04.080
Okay! Sure!

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:30.880
Why the hell would they
need to call us to the factory?

00:19:30.880 --> 00:19:33.950
They must've screwed something up.

00:19:33.950 --> 00:19:36.440
They can never do anything right.

00:19:37.690 --> 00:19:40.350
You're finally able to talk that way, too...

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:53.970
Tifosi to Modena 01.

00:19:53.970 --> 00:19:56.940
Target heading south
on the Road of Italy.

00:19:56.940 --> 00:20:02.880
Contact with 01 in 20 seconds.
No civilian cars within 200 meters.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:06.750
Are you still seeing that French woman?

00:20:06.750 --> 00:20:09.750
Aline? Of course.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:14.920
What's so good about French women?
Stick with women from Milan.

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:21.770
Modena 01 to 04 and 05. All set?

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:22.930
Yeah.

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:24.960
Ready.

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:30.710
Listen, Rico.
Promise me you'll do it just like in training.

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:40.690
Don't kill anyone.

00:20:40.690 --> 00:20:41.670
Yes, sir.

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:56.370
Damn, that was close!

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:58.360
Keep your head down, Vinci!

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:12.550
An armored car?!

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:23.750
What?!

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:28.730
Damn you!

00:21:56.660 --> 00:21:57.900
Angelica.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.330
Y-Yes, sir?!

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:02.470
Well? Are you feeling all right?

00:22:02.470 --> 00:22:04.540
I'm fine...

00:22:04.540 --> 00:22:08.170
I'm sorry, Marco-san. I failed...

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:11.280
There's nothing you could've
done to an armored Ferrari.

00:22:11.280 --> 00:22:15.350
But you moved fast, and you hit it spot-on.

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:17.440
Great job.

00:22:41.370 --> 00:22:46.400
What? Am I having
a bad dream or something?

00:22:49.350 --> 00:22:52.440
What a fucked-up world...

00:22:54.690 --> 00:22:56.680
Rico!

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:06.330
I'm sorry, Angelica. I broke my promise.

00:23:06.330 --> 00:23:11.800
No, that's okay! Marco-san
praised me! He said I did a great job!

00:23:11.800 --> 00:23:15.740
Really? That's great, Angelica!

00:23:42.630 --> 00:23:57.480
A doll without a heart,
born from warm hands

00:23:57.480 --> 00:24:07.160
I neither smile nor talk

00:24:07.160 --> 00:24:15.430
I want you to hear about
these feelings someday,

00:24:15.430 --> 00:24:23.340
though they can't be put into words

00:24:23.340 --> 00:24:31.420
I'll summon all my strength

00:24:31.420 --> 00:24:43.350
to know what it means to live

00:25:00.450 --> 00:25:05.530
"Evanescence and Reminiscence"
